ary_generated_at":null,"ai_relevance_score":null,"key_technologies":null,"citation_count":371,"is_key_spec":1,"created_at":"2026-07-24 23:02:13"},{"id":5,"spec_number":"TS 38.300","spec_id":"38.300","type":"TS","series":"38","title":"NR and NG-RAN Overall Description","technology":"5G NR","category":"Architecture","network_layer":"Radio Access Network","status":"Active","release":"Rel-17","version":"17.4.0","last_updated":"2023-04-05","ftp_url":"https://www.3gpp.org/ftp/Specs/archive/38_series/38.300/","ai_summary":null,"ai_summary_generated_at":null,"ai_relevance_score":null,"key_technologies":null,"citation_count":360,"is_key_spec":1,"created_at":"2026-07-24 23:02:13"},{"id":6,"spec_number":"TS 36.300","spec_id":"36.300","type":"TS","series":"36","title":"E-UTRA and E-UTRAN Overall Description","technology":"LTE","category":"Architecture","network_layer":"Radio Access Network","status":"Active","release":"Rel-17","version":"17.3.0","last_updated":"2023-01-11","ftp_url":"https://www.3gpp.org/ftp/Specs/archive/36_series/36.300/","ai_summary":"# 3GPP TS 36.300 — E-UTRA and E-UTRAN Overall Description\n\n## What It Specifies\nThe architectural reference document for LTE RAN. Defines the overall E-UTRAN architecture, functional split between nodes, and the protocols and procedures that bind the system together. It's the entry point before diving into detailed procedure specs (36.304, 36.321, 36.331, etc.).\n\n## Key Interfaces Defined\n- **X2**: eNB-to-eNB interface — handover signaling, load management, interference coordination (eICIC)\n- **S1-MME**: eNB-to-MME control plane (S1AP)\n- **S1-U**: eNB-to-S-GW user plane (GTP-U)\n- **LTE-Uu**: Air interface between UE and eNB\n\n## Key Procedures Specified (at architecture level)\n- Intra/inter-frequency and inter-RAT handover flows\n- S1 and X2 setup and reset procedures\n- Paging and cell search architecture\n- RRC states (RRC_IDLE, RRC_CONNECTED) and state transitions\n- MBMS architecture and bearer handling\n- Carrier aggregation and dual connectivity (eNB-MeNB/SeNB split)\n- SON functions: ANR, MLB, MRO\n- Security architecture (AS/NAS separation)\n\n## When a RAN Engineer Uses It\n- **Network design**: Understanding functional splits when planning X2 mesh topology or S1 flex configurations\n- **Integration**: Validating eNB interconnect setup (X2/S1 establishment sequences)\n- **Dual connectivity / ENDC baseline**: Understanding MeNB/SeNB architecture before referencing 37.340\n- **Troubleshooting**: Confirming expected handover trigger logic or paging flow architecture before tracing at the procedure level\n- **Spec navigation**: Identifying which detailed spec owns a specific procedure\n\n**Bottom line**: Read this first. It's the map before the territory.","ai_summary_generated_at":"2026-07-25T01:35:36.992Z","ai_relevance_score":95,"key_technologies":null,"citation_count":349,"is_key_spec":1,"created_at":"2026-07-24 23:02:13"},{"id":7,"spec_number":"TS 38.213","spec_id":"38.213","type":"TS","series":"38","title":"NR Physical Layer Procedures for Control","technology":"5G NR","category":"Physical Layer","network_layer":"Radio Access Network","status":"Active","release":"Rel-17","version":"17.5.0","last_updated":"2023-06-23","ftp_url":"https://www.3gpp.org/ftp/Specs/archive/38_series/38.213/","ai_summary":null,"ai_summary_generated_at":null,"ai_relevance_score":null,"key_technologies":null,"citation_count":338,"is_key_spec":1,"created_at":"2026-07-24 23:02:13"},{"id":8,"spec_number":"TS 38.211","spec_id":"38.211","type":"TS","series":"38","title":"NR Physical Channels and Modulation","technology":"5G NR","category":"Physical Layer","network_layer":"Radio Access Network","status":"Active","release":"Rel-17","version":"17.5.0","last_updated":"2023-06-23","ftp_url":"https://www.3gpp.org/ftp/Specs/archive/38_series/38.211/","ai_summary":null,"ai_summary_generated_at":null,"ai_relevance_score":null,"key_technologies":null,"citation_count":327,"is_key_spec":1,"created_at":"2026-07